{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"d58b8427d48bdd6a","x":-360,"y":-580,"width":860,"height":300,"type":"text","text":"## Baseball App: \n### Goal:\n- Build an app (iPhone, Android, and web) where tool can read and ingest input from the user and provide a feedback/analysis to user\n- Leveraging AI techniques, user will receive feedback on how they can fix their batting and pitching mechanism from AI analysis. All feedbacks must derive from professional's samples and analysis will be compared based on baseline (user) vs trained sample (Professional Athlete's sample)\n- Deploy the app at the lowest cost as possible where kids to adult can use it without budget problem"},
		{"id":"55a48c86abf10f93","x":-100,"y":-200,"width":269,"height":220,"type":"text","text":"## Project List\n1. Batting\n2. Pitching\n3. Tennis\n4. Golf"},
		{"id":"9ae84c2d86c5bcdd","x":-1140,"y":160,"width":767,"height":504,"type":"text","text":"## Batting Part\n\n### 타자의 세부학적 세그먼트\n1. 파워 유형의 타자 (거포형 혹은 홈런 타자, 삼진율이 많음)\n\t1. 예를 들어 Aaron Judge, Shohei Ohtani, Cal Raleigh, Ken Griffey Jr, Kyle Schwarber, Yordan Alvarez, Junior Caminero, James Wood, and etc \n2. 컨택 유형의 타자 (안타 많이 치고 똑딱이 유형, 삼진율이 적음)\n\t1. 예를 들어 Jung hoo Lee, Ichiro Suzuki, Luis Arraez, Nico Hoerner, Chandler Simpson, Ernie Clement, Ildemaro Vargas\n3. 중장거리의 타자/Gap hitter (2루타 많이 치는 애들, 골고루 잘침)\n\t1. 예를 들어 Otto Lopez, Matt Olson, Ceddanne Rafaela, Alec Burleson, Ernie Clement, Rafael Devers, Freddie Freeman, Juan Soto\n### Technical session:\n**타자의 세부학적 세그먼트에 따라 개별로 학습과 분석을 따야함**\n1. 2D & 3D Skeleton pose estimation\n2. Bat Tracking \n\t1. Bat speed estimation\n\t2. Bat path estimation\n3. Launch Angle\n4. Hard hit distribution\n5. Contact point\n6. Hit into play\n### User Input:\n- 타자 세부학적 세그먼트 (파워, 컨택, 중장거리 중 선택)\n- 신체 스펙 (키 와 몸무게)\n- 우타 혹은 좌타\n- 타격 비디오"},
		{"id":"ba3c0472a96259fe","x":-132,"y":161,"width":572,"height":503,"type":"text","text":"## Pitching Part\n### 투수의 세부학적 세그먼트\n1. 오버핸드 (Overhand) - 머리 위에서 아래로 내리꽂듯 공을 던지는 유형\n\t1. 예를 들어 Cam schlittler, Gerrit Cole, Trey Yesavage, Adolis Chapman, Mason Miller, and etc\n2. 쓰리쿼터 (Three-quarter) - 오버핸드와 사이드암의 중간 각도로 던지는 유형, 가장 흔한 투구폼\n\t1. 예를 들어 Ohtani Shohei, Bryan Woo, Luis Castillo, Yoshinobu Yamamoto\n3. 사이드암 (Side-arm) - 팔을 옆으로 뻗어 수평에 가까운 각도로 던지는 유형\n4. 언더핸드 (Underhand) - 팔을 아래에서 위로 퍼올리듯 낮게 던지는 유형\n\n### Technical Session\n#### 1. Key Sequence:\n1. Ground\n2. Legs\n3. Pelvis\n4. Trunk\n5. Shoulder,\n6. Elbow\n7. Hand\n8. Release the ball\n- Slow motion is ideal like 120-240 fps and capture several pitches rather than judging one delivery\n#### 2. Mark the major events\nBefore evaluating mechanics, identify these frames:\n1. First movement\n2. Peak leg lift\n3. Hand separation\n4. Maximum stride or “foot hover”\n5. Lead-foot contact\n6. Maximum external rotation\n7. Ball release\n8. Maximum lead-knee extension\n9. Finish\n#### 3. Break the delivery into phases\n\n|Phase|What to examine|Why it matters|\n|---|---|---|\n|**Set-up**|Foot position, posture, grip, head position, tension, consistency|Establishes a repeatable starting point. Unnecessary tension can interfere with rhythm and movement.|\n|**Gather and leg lift**|Balance, controlled center of mass, pelvis loading, head stability, tempo|The pitcher must organize the body over the back leg before moving forcefully toward the plate. “Balance” should be dynamic, not a prolonged pause.|\n|**Move down the mound**|Hip leading, center-of-mass direction, rear-leg loading, stride tempo|Good pitchers begin creating momentum while maintaining enough control to sequence the delivery.|\n|**Hand separation and arm path**|When the hands separate, smoothness of the arm path, excess tension or hesitation|The throwing arm must arrive on time with the lower body. Arm timing is usually more important than copying a particular arm-path shape.|\n|**Stride and lead-foot contact**|Stride direction, foot angle, lead-knee flexion, posture, pelvis orientation|Foot contact creates the base against which the trunk and throwing arm accelerate. Poor direction can make command and rotation less consistent.|\n|**Hip–shoulder sequencing**|Pelvis beginning to rotate before the upper trunk, shoulders remaining controlled until landing|This transfers energy from the lower body into the torso. Opening everything simultaneously often reduces efficient energy transfer.|\n|**Arm-cocking phase**|Elbow relationship to the shoulder line, shoulder rotation, forearm progression, trunk position|The arm must coordinate with trunk rotation. Being substantially early or late can reduce velocity, command, or recovery time.|\n|**Acceleration and release**|Trunk rotation, forward trunk movement, lead-leg stabilization, head position, release location|This is where accumulated energy reaches the ball. Release consistency strongly influences command and pitch shape.|\n|**Deceleration**|Arm continuing across the body, trunk moving forward, rear leg coming through|The body must safely absorb the high forces created during acceleration. Abrupt stopping is generally undesirable.|\n|**Finish and fielding position**|Overall control, balance, direction, recovery, ability to defend the position|The finish reveals whether momentum was transferred and absorbed smoothly. It should not be judged only by whether the pitcher “stands tall.”|\n\n### User Input:\n- Types of throwing hand (Lefty or righty) and mechanism (overhand, sidearm, or etc)\n- 신체 스펙 (키와 몸무게)\n- Pitching Video"}
	],
